WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.775
After AI 410, this is what you can build with AI.

2
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.900
This is a real app, running live: a support assistant for an outdoor gear store.

3
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:19.625
Ask about returns, and it answers from the store's own policy documents, not from guesswork.

4
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:30.925
Ask for a total, and it decides to call its calculator tool, instead of doing the math in its head.

5
00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:34.000
And every step it takes can be traced.

6
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.025
Ask about something the documents don't cover, and it says it doesn't know.

7
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.750
Then add a new rental sheet.

8
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.050
A background worker reads it, and seconds later, the assistant can answer.

9
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.700
The same app runs on a phone, through a mobile client you build too.

10
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.175
You build each piece in AI 410, across four hands-on units.

11
00:01:26.625 --> 00:01:29.175
Then your team builds an app of its own.

12
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.525
AI 410: AI Engineering.

13
00:01:35.975 --> 00:01:40.200
Part of the BS in AI at City University of Seattle.

14
00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:43.000
See the course at the link on screen.
